> The Project Management Committee (PMC) for Apache Kafka is pleased to
> announce Jiunn-Yang Huang as a new Kafka committer.
>
> Jiunn-Yang has been one of the most active contributors to the project,
> leading in commits in 2025 with over 200 commits and 170 reviews. He has
> consistently taken on essential but often overlooked work, from unifying
> configuration validation (KIP-1161) to fixing critical bugs in the
> AsyncConsumer and resolving long-standing issues ahead of the 4.0 release=
.
> His patience, persistence, and attention to detail have made the project
> more consistent and reliable.
>
> Beyond code, Jiunn-Yang is an active community advocate, sharing Kafka 4.=
0
> with users in Beijing and Taipei and regularly helping contributors and
> users troubleshoot in community meetups.
>
> Please join me in welcoming and congratulating Jiunn-Yang!
>
> Chia-Ping Tsai
> On behalf of the Apache Kafka PMC
>

--0000000000006b85430659a60bf4--

