Good Afternoon,
Am looking to control log4j2 output produced by Kafka...but am having a lit=
tle difficultly getting this to work as expected.

During the kafka producer startup I've added this command:  -Dlog4j2.config=
urationFile=3D/<whatever>/kafka/producers/log4j2.properties

I've created a log4j2.properties file as follows:

# Root Logger
rootLogger=3DINFO, STDERR

# Direct log messages to stderr
appender.console.type =3D Console
appender.console.name =3D STDERR
appender.console.layout.type =3D PatternLayout
appender.console.layout.pattern =3D [%-5level] %d{yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.SSS} =
[%t] %C{1} - %msg%n

Yet, when I look at STDERR am not seeing the desired messages. Do I need to=
 configure slf4j instead or in conjunction?  Anything I'm possibly doing wr=
ong?

Anyone with experience on customizing kafka message logging, will to chime =
in?

Thank You,
--Alex


